# The first line that is not a comment is what `lab/evolve/next-run.sh` does
# when it is given no argument: "seed N" (a new run - the last one's records
# archived first), "compare" (every run's front here measured again in one
# session), "experiment TOOL ARGS" (a tracked tool in lab/evolve/, given every
# database here) or "none" (pull and stop). compare and experiment archive
# nothing. Each iteration sets it for the bundle it hands over (Iteration 22).
#
# Iteration 28: none - the owner asked for as few laptop runs as possible;
# what needs the laptop's clock is batched for one session later (GOALS.md).
#
# Iteration 35: "A then B" runs B when A has finished and packed - one
# sitting, two packs. Seed 6: the first run with the tests that keep their
# value and SWAP n + (Iterations 33-34) for the evolver to weigh; then every
# front here, seeds 3-6, measured again in one session on two CPUs.
seed 6 then experiment compare-fronts.py --rounds 10 --cpus 2,8
